          "explanation": {
            "content": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Each nitrogen has a lone pair that can bond to a metal ion. Because the single bonds in the structure can rotate, this ligand is “flexible” and can “wrap” around the metal with N connections in three places. Diethlyenetriamine is a tridentate ligand."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2830368746",
                "type": "p"
              }
